
`native/` holds the AUnit tests for ImplementScraper/InterfaceScraper
(../lib/KilverbakbesturingCore/src/), run natively (no Teensy attached):

- `native/tests/` -- one `test_<ClassName>.cpp` per class under test.
- `native/support/` -- a small, self-contained set of Arduino-shaped stubs
  (Print/Stream/EEPROM/Arduino.h/etc.), not a real EpoxyDuino dependency, plus
  `native_main.cpp` (the host `int main()` entry point). These stand in for
  the Arduino framework and MeijWorks Libs' `VehicleSensors`/`InterfaceI2CLCD`
  only: `GuidanceSource` and `DistanceBetween()` (MeijWorks Libs/
  VehicleGuidance, `GuidanceSource.hpp` and `GuidanceGeometry.hpp`) are the
  real header-only code, so this module's leveling calculation runs on the
  same flat local-tangent-plane distances the board computes. The channels
  that feed the source on the board have their suites in Ploegbesturing
  Isobus' native build.
- `native/KilverbakbesturingIsobusNativeTests.cpp` -- the single AUnit driver
  (`setup()`/`loop()`), matching Ploegbesturing's/Pootmachinebesturing's/
  Spuitcomputer SP's `*NativeTests.cpp` pattern. Every `test_*.cpp`
  file only registers `test(...)` blocks; none of them define `setup()`/
  `loop()` themselves, so they all link into one combined binary instead of
  one binary per test file.
- `native/run_tests_msvc.ps1` -- MSVC fallback for Windows without GCC.

```
pio run -e native
.pio/build/native/program(.exe)
```

Needs a real host C++17 compiler on PATH (g++ or clang++) -- on Windows
without one, use test\native\run_tests_msvc.ps1 instead, which builds and
runs the same combined binary via MSVC directly. That script passes
`/Zc:preprocessor` -- MSVC's legacy preprocessor mishandles AUnit's
`test(SuiteName, testName)` argument-count dispatch, which every test in
this project uses (matching this family's convention: groups each test's
display name under the class it exercises, e.g.
`ImplementScraper_calculateDistances_degenerateReferencePoints_fallsBackToZero`,
`InterfaceScraper_update_staleGgaFix_selectsHold`).

## Known gaps

- `CalibrationScraper` is a step runner since NeptuneGPS_Triton#289 and is
  tested here, screen by screen, through the recording LCD stub
  (`support/InterfaceI2CLCD.hpp`, the plough's) and the button pins; its
  settings table has `test_ScraperSettings.cpp`. What the wizard draws while
  a value is being edited is checked on the cells that carry the value.
- `ImplementScraper::getActualPosition()`'s divide-by-zero guard (two
  calibration points holding the same reading) has no public setter to
  construct that state directly -- `positionCalibrationData` is only settable
  through `SetPositionCalibrationData()`, which reads a *live* `analogRead()`,
  and the whole sensored code path is `#ifndef NOSENS`-gated (dead on every
  board built today; this production unit has no position sensor at all,
  matching the legacy source's `NOSENS` default). Same gap Spuitcomputer
  SP's PWM-calibration guard has, for the same reason.
- `InterfaceScraper::UpdateScreen()` (LCD rendering) compiles as part of
  `InterfaceScraper.cpp` (needed since `CheckButtons()`/`Update()`, which
  *are* tested, live in the same file) but its output isn't asserted on by
  any test -- `test/native/support/InterfaceI2CLCD.hpp`'s `WriteBuffer`/
  `WriteScreen` are no-ops.
- Since #291 the suite is built with `-D ISOBUS` on the real AgIsoStack,
  compiled for the host as in Ploegbesturing Isobus: `test_VTObjectPool.cpp`
  walks the pool object by object, and `test_ScraperVtWorkingSet.cpp` drives
  the working set's keys (one test through `IsobusVtInterface`'s own key
  listener), its screen values and the reference page;
  `test_ScraperVtCalibration.cpp` the calibration page (#292). What the VT itself
  draws is not tested here: no VT server runs off-target, so the sends to a
  client go nowhere, and `UpdateValues()` returns before it sends. The values
  it sends come from `ComputeScreenValues()`, which is tested. The serial
  builds' settings table (no PreferredVt line) is no longer built natively.
  `ScraperName.hpp` and the ISOBUS half of `src/main.cpp` are only compiled for
  the board; the shared ISOBUS layer (MeijWorks Libs/IsobusImplement) is tested
  in Ploegbesturing Isobus' native build.
- None of the four board envs has run on hardware yet (NeptuneGPS_Triton#288,
  #293): only `pio run` cross-compiles.
- The Arduino Micro, the Micro/Leonardo "voorserie" board and the Teensy
  3.5/3.6 protoboard keep their `#ifdef` branches in the config headers, as in
  Kilverbakbesturing, without a buildable env.

More information about PlatformIO Unit Testing (not used here -- pio test's
own Unity-based runner doesn't understand this project's AUnit setup):
- https://docs.platformio.org/en/latest/advanced/unit-testing/index.html
